>> title: Carrot Cake
>> part: Desserts

= Recipe

Whisk together the flour, baking soda, baking powder, salt, cinnamon, nutmeg, and ginger in a medium bowl.

@all-purpose flour{280%g|2.25%cup}
@baking soda{2%tsp}
@baking powder{1%tsp}
@salt{1/2%tsp}
@ground cinnamon{1.5%tsp}
@ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}
@ground ginger{1/4%tsp}

In a large bowl, whisk the granulated sugar, molasses, oil, and eggs together until completely smooth and evenly colored.

@granulated sugar{400%g|2%cup}
@molasses{1-1.5%tbsp}
@neutral oil{215%g|1%cup}
@eggs, room temperature{4}

Fold the dry ingredients into the wet mixture until just combined. Gently fold in the grated carrots.

@finely grated carrots (about 1 lb whole){330%g|3%cup}

Pour the batter into a prepared {{9 x 13%}} pan. Bake at {{350%°F}} for 35-40 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Cool completely in the pan on a wire rack.

= Frosting

Beat the cream cheese and butter together until completely smooth. Add the powdered sugar, vanilla, and salt, beating until fluffy. Spread evenly over the cooled cake.

@cream cheese, softened{226%g|8%oz}
@unsalted butter, softened{1%stick|115%g}
@powdered sugar{360-480%g|3-4%cup}
@vanilla extract{1%tsp}
@salt{1%pinch}
